// SOUNDNESS QUEUE row boxref_sized_struct_deref_coercion_missing (tier 3, `refuses`).
// A LEGAL program is refused: `&b` where `b: Box<A>` for an ordinary SIZED struct `A`,
// passed to a `&A` parameter, is Rust's deref coercion and logosc refuses it with
//   error [fn main]: call to 'rd' arg 1: expected &A, got &Box<A>
// compile rc 1, no object file.
//
// legality: MEASURED, rustc 1.98.1 --edition 2024 compiles and runs the twin at exit 0
// (src/compiler/probes/2026-09-15h-boxdynref/rust/r08_box_concrete.rs).
//
// FOUND 2026-09-15h-boxdynref as counter-example ce08, guarding the `&Box<S>` half of
// the owner's ruling. PRE-EXISTING — measured identical on base binary
// d8d756468efca2d6 43 and on the landed binary 9e1bf6ab1d91ea72 43, so this round
// neither caused nor repaired it.
// ⚠ IT CONTRADICTS A SPEC CLAUSE: `coerce.deref.box-struct-borrow` claimed `&Box<S>`
// borrows as `&S`. It does so ONLY for a custom-DST (owning DstRef) `S` — the sized
// case was never implemented. The clause's scope was corrected in the same commit
// (docs/spec/types.md + tools/spec-extract/rules/sema/sema_expr/lower_unary.part1.json);
// the DEFECT is left open here rather than repaired inside a priced refusal landing.
package boxref_sized_struct_deref_coercion_missing;
use logos.mem.boxed;

struct A { x: i64 }

fn rd(a: &A) -> i64 { return a.x; }

fn main() -> i32 {
    let b: Box<A> = box_new(A { x: 42i64 });
    if rd(&b) != 42i64 { return 3i32; }
    return 0i32;
}
